DTSTAMP:20260724T105730Z
DTSTART:20260725T213000Z
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate l
	inks. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. \nAbout the Perfor
	mer\nTony Rock is a comedian\, actor\, and producer — the younger brother 
	of Chris Rock — who has built his own legendary career in stand-up and tel
	evision. He hosted HBO’s All Def Comedy\, BET’s Apollo Live\, and co-starr
	ed in CBS’ Living Biblically. He is also the founder of the MyROCK Diabete
	s Foundation. \nEvent Details\nDate: Saturday\, July 25\, 2026 \nTime: 9:3
	0 PM (Late Show) \nVenue: Arlington Improv\, 309 Curtis Mathes Way #147\, 
	Arlington\, TX 76018 \nAge Restriction: 18+ \nPrice Range: $25 to $70 per 
	person \nAbout the Venue\nArlington Improv is located in the Highlands Sho
	pping Center in Arlington\, TX\, across from Torchy’s Tacos. An intimate c
	omedy club with a full bar\, restaurant\, and Black Dog Pizza Arcade featu
	ring 30+ local craft beers. Seating is assigned based on date of purchase.
	 \nWhat to Expect\nTony Rock closes out Saturday night at Arlington Improv
	 with a full late-show headlining set. Expect sharp wit\, personal stories
	\, and commanding stage presence — the perfect way to end your Saturday ni
	ght. \nThis is an 18+ event. Food and beverage service ends approximately 
	45 minutes into the show. All sales are final. \nTicket Information\nTicke
	ts range from $25 to $70 per person. Purchase official tickets or find res
	ale options below. \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets\n\nhttps://comedycalen
	dar.com/event/tony-rock-live-at-arlington-improv-saturday-late/\n\nFrom Co
	medy Calendar
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/tony-rock-live-at-arlington-improv-sat
	urday-late/
